    "text": "```json\n{\"status\":\"ready_to_execute\",\"notes\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"edge_count\":0}\n```\nCOMPLIANCE:\nScene ID: SC_006_006\nAllowed events: Rhea crafts the Null-Value Token using her remaining high-tier materials. The party escapes the tollbooth using the pathing glitch (callback). Rhea remains at 1 Stamina, Vance remains at 10 HP.\nForbidden milestones: None violated.\n\nCurrent arm-side / inventory facts: \n- Vance holds Rebar in hand_right.\n- Rhea holds nothing in hand_left.\n- Rhea has Heavy Iron Ingot and Crystallized Experience in system_inventory.\n\nDurable changes committed:\n- ITEM_heavy_iron_ingot consumed (transferred to world).\n- ITEM_crystallized_experience consumed (transferred to world).\n- ITEM_null_value_token created and placed in Rhea's hand_left.\n- System inventory contents updated to reflect consumed items.\n\nAPPEARANCE_CHECK:\n- rhea_mercer: singed arm hair\n- vance_harrow: heavily blistered hands\n- unit_734: smoking chassis\n\nPROSE:\nAfter navigating the treacherous gray dunes of the Ash Wastes, the party reached the jagged outskirts of the administrative hub and immediately took cover behind a massive basalt boulder.\n\nVance slumped against the stone, his breath rattling in his chest as he gripped his Rebar with heavily blistered hands. His health bar was a razor-thin red line, still frozen at exactly 10 HP. Escaping the tollbooth had been a miracle of bad programming\u2014Rhea\u2019s desperate physics exploit of jamming Unit 734 into the doorframe had completely broken the hounds' pathing AI, letting them slip past the glitched enemies.\n\nRhea slid down the boulder next to the mechanical construct, its smoking chassis venting thin plumes of gray exhaust into the air. She rubbed her bare forearms, the singed arm hair still smelling faintly of ozone. Her own Stamina was locked at a miserable 1, the *Exhaustion (Severe)* status effect making every blink feel like lifting weights. But she couldn't stop. They were at the threshold.\n\nShe opened her interface.\n\n[System Inventory Accessed.]\n\nReaching into the digital space, she withdrew the Heavy Iron Ingot. It hit the ash-covered ground with a dull, heavy thud. Next, she pulled out the Crystallized Experience\u2014a jagged shard of pure, refunded value that pulsed with a violent purple light. These were the high-tier materials she needed.\n\nShe placed the glowing shard directly on top of the dense iron block.\n\n[Crafting Interface Initialized.]\n\n[Warning: Incompatible Materials.]\n\nShe didn\u2019t need them to be compatible. She needed them to break the math. Using the administrative weight of her *Audit Compliance (Red-Tier)* debuff, she forced a manual synthesis, grinding the pure numerical value of the experience into the physical density of the iron to create a logical paradox.\n\n[Override Authorized: Audit Compliance Active.]\n\n[Consuming: Heavy Iron Ingot (x1), Crystallized Experience (x1)]\n\nThe purple light flared, violently compressing the iron until both items collapsed into a single point of absolute darkness. When the light faded, a heavy, light-swallowing coin rested in the ash.\n\n[Item Created: Null-Value Token.]\n\nRhea scooped the cold coin up with her left hand.\n\nShe had successfully crafted the Null-Value Token. With her high-tier materials consumed in the paradox, Vance pushed himself off the rock, and the party prepared for the final breach.\n\nSTATE_PATCH:\n```json\n{\n  \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"world_updates\": {\n    \"location\": \"LOC_ADMINISTRATIVE_HUB_OUTSKIRTS\"\n  },\n  \"character_updates\": [\n    {\n      \"character_id\": \"rhea_mercer\",\n      \"chapter\": 6,\n      \"scene\": 6,\n      \"inventory\": [\n        {\n          \"container\": \"blazer_pocket_left\",\n          \"item\": \"ITEM_administrative_coordinate_chip\",\n          \"status\": \"stowed\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"container\": \"blazer_pocket_left\",\n          \"item\": \"ITEM_obsidian_shard\